# List & Table Layout Patterns

## Pattern Recognition Guide

When analyzing list and table designs, look for these common patterns:

### 1. Basic List Layout
```tsx
<div className="rounded-lg border">
  <div className="p-4 border-b bg-muted/40">
    <div className="flex items-center justify-between">
      <h2 className="font-semibold">List Title</h2>
      <div className="flex items-center gap-4">
        <Search />
        <FilterDropdown />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  
  <div className="divide-y">
    {items.map(item => (
      <div key={item.id} className="p-4 hover:bg-muted/50">
        <div className="flex items-center justify-between">
          <div className="flex items-center gap-4">
            <Avatar />
            <div>
              <p className="font-medium">{item.title}</p>
              <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">{item.description}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <Button variant="ghost" size="icon">
            <MoreVertical className="h-4 w-4" />
          </Button>
        </div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
</div>
```

### 2. Advanced Table Layout
```tsx
<div className="rounded-lg border">
  {/* Table Header */}
  <div className="p-4 border-b bg-muted/40">
    <div className="flex items-center justify-between">
      <div className="flex items-center gap-4">
        <h2 className="font-semibold">Table Title</h2>
        <Badge>{items.length} items</Badge>
      </div>
      <div className="flex items-center gap-4">
        <Search />
        <FilterDropdown />
        <Button>
          <Plus className="h-4 w-4 mr-2" />
          Add New
        </Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  
  {/* Table Content */}
  <Table>
    <TableHeader>
      <TableRow>
        <TableHead className="w-[40px]">
          <Checkbox />
        </TableHead>
        <TableHead>Name</TableHead>
        <TableHead>Status</TableHead>
        <TableHead className="text-right">Actions</TableHead>
      </TableRow>
    </TableHeader>
    <TableBody>
      {items.map(item => (
        <TableRow key={item.id}>
          <TableCell>
            <Checkbox />
          </TableCell>
          <TableCell>
            <div className="flex items-center gap-4">
              <Avatar />
              <div>
                <p className="font-medium">{item.name}</p>
                <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">{item.email}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </TableCell>
          <TableCell>
            <Badge>{item.status}</Badge>
          </TableCell>
          <TableCell className="text-right">
            <Button variant="ghost" size="icon">
              <MoreVertical className="h-4 w-4" />
            </Button>
          </TableCell>
        </TableRow>
      ))}
    </TableBody>
  </Table>
  
  {/* Table Footer */}
  <div className="p-4 border-t">
    <div className="flex items-center justify-between">
      <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        Showing 1-10 of 100 items
      </p>
      <Pagination />
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

### 3. Grid List Layout
```tsx
<div className="space-y-4">
  {/* Header */}
  <div className="flex items-center justify-between">
    <h2 className="font-semibold">Grid List</h2>
    <div className="flex items-center gap-4">
      <ViewToggle />
      <FilterDropdown />
    </div>
  </div>
  
  {/* Grid */}
  <div className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 xl:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
    {items.map(item => (
      <Card key={item.id}>
        <CardHeader>
          <div className="aspect-video relative rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
            <Image
              src={item.image}
              alt={item.title}
              fill
              className="object-cover"
            />
          </div>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent className="space-y-2">
          <h3 className="font-medium">{item.title}</h3>
          <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">{item.description}</p>
        </CardContent>
        <CardFooter>
          <Button variant="ghost" className="w-full">
            View Details
          </Button>
        </CardFooter>
      </Card>
    ))}
  </div>
  
  {/* Footer */}
  <div className="flex items-center justify-between">
    <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      Showing 1-12 of 100 items
    </p>
    <Pagination />
  </div>
</div>
```

### Pattern Recognition Steps

1. **List Type Identification**
   - Simple list vs table vs grid
   - Data complexity and relationships
   - Interactive requirements

2. **Header Components**
   - Search and filtering
   - Bulk actions
   - View toggles

3. **Content Structure**
   - Primary and secondary information
   - Action placement
   - Status indicators

4. **Interactive Elements**
   - Row/item actions
   - Bulk selection
   - Inline editing

5. **Footer Components**
   - Pagination
   - Summary information
   - Batch actions

### Best Practices

1. **Responsive Behavior**
   - Stack on mobile
   - Horizontal scroll for tables
   - Adjust grid columns

2. **Loading States**
   - Skeleton loading
   - Progressive loading
   - Load more vs pagination

3. **Empty States**
   - Helpful messaging
   - Clear actions
   - Placeholder content

4. **Selection States**
   - Clear indicators
   - Bulk actions
   - Selection persistence

Remember: Lists and tables should make data exploration and manipulation intuitive. Layout should support quick scanning and efficient interaction. 